<title>NETHERLANDS: Aegon nine month total net up 16.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Aegon nine month total net up 16.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>First nine-months 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     4.15 vs   3.59</p>
<p>    Total net profit (billions)	1.10 vs   0.94</p>
<p>    Total revenues (billions)	 18.21 vs  15.53</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast insurance company Aegon NV would make nine month total net profits of 1.05-1.15 billion guilders.  </p>
<p>Total benefits &amp; expenses (billion) 16.80  vs 14.30</p>
<p>Breakdown on net income:</p>
<p>    - Life insurance			  1,133  vs  984</p>
<p>    - Accident and health		     114  vs  110</p>
<p>    - General insurance			  47  vs   35</p>
<p>    - Banking activities			124  vs  102</p>
<p>    - Other activities		     loss 4  vs    2 profit</p>
<p>    Tax charges				   314  vs  290</p>
<p>    Interest (billions)			   1.08  vs    1.06</p>
<p>Breakdown of total revenues by sector:</p>
<p>    - Life insurance (billions)		 9.51  vs    7.52</p>
<p>    - Accident and health (billions)	  1.74  vs    1.49</p>
<p>    - General insurance (billions)	    1.22  vs    1.21</p>
<p>    - Investment income (billions)	    4.83  vs    4.44</p>
<p>    - Income from banking			909    vs  885</p>
<p>    Commission and expenses (billions)	2.52  vs    2.19</p>
<p>    Shareholders equity (billions)	   10.39  vs    8.17</p>
<p>    Subordinated loans (billions)	     4.22  vs    3.61</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
